rn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f128a886574e5ea88775535ff930828ec5090d4f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f128a886574e5ea88775535ff930828ec5090d4f.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued September 15 at 6:34PM MDT until September 15 at 9:30PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Mesa County in west central Colorado...\nCentral Grand County in east central Utah...\nThis includes the I-70 corridor between Crescent Junction, in Utah,\nand Grand Junction, in Colorado.\n\n* WHEN...Until 930 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry arroyos. Dangerous flows\nover low-water crossings. Ponding of water in urban or other areas\nis occurring or is imminent.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 632 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1.5 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFruita, Mack, Loma and Redlands.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-15T21:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Mesa, CO; Grand, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9240c195bbbaffebcf719c01f9691af687ce6bf8.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9240c195bbbaffebcf719c01f9691af687ce6bf8.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued September 15 at 6:32PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"At 632 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 12\nmiles north of Fruita, or 18 miles northwest of Grand Junction,\nmoving east at 20 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and half inch hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nThis storm will remain over mainly rural areas of northwestern Mesa\nCounty.","ends":"2026-09-15T19:00:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus; Grand Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1c30a46c0a4d80ffb4e827140d8823c0af2678a9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1c30a46c0a4d80ffb4e827140d8823c0af2678a9.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued September 15 at 6:25PM MDT until September 15 at 9:30PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorthwestern Mesa County in west central Colorado...\n\n* Until 930 PM MDT.\n\n* At 625 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 0.5 and 1 inch of rain\nhas fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1 to 3 inches in 1 hour.\nFlash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Northwestern Mesa County, including I-70\nbetween mile marker 5 and mile marker 10.","ends":"2026-09-15T21:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mesa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.91c16a794b99790d468ea61d98923cebb31c982f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.91c16a794b99790d468ea61d98923cebb31c982f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-16T00:17:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 160017 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 617 PM MDT Tue Sep 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - There is a chance for strong to severe storms over the next few days, capable of producing hail, gusty winds, and heavy rainfall. - Moderate to heavy rainfall could lead to localized flash flooding, rockfalls, and mudslides at times this week. - Flood Watc","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-15T19:00:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Critical fire weather conditions will not be met as subtropical moisture continues to feed into the 4 Corners and Central Rockies region this week. Daily and nightly shower and thunderstorm activity can be anticipated with some storms producing gusty outflow winds and containing moderate to heavy rainfall rates. Widespread wetting rainfall appears likely through the week. ...GUSTY ER","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"frt03","station_name":"CSU Fruita Exp Station","distance_km":3.8,"soil_temp_5cm_f":76.57,"soil_temp_15cm_f":75.33,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":7.6,"wind_speed_mph":6.78,"air_temp_f":68.67,"relative_humidity":0.665,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/frt03"},"aviation":{"icao":"KGJT","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KGJT 152353Z 13018G24KT 10SM CLR 27/11 A3000 RMK AO2 LTG DSNT W AND NW SLP094 60009 T02720106 10283 20217 56017","temp_f":81,"wind_dir":130,"wind_kt":18,"gust_kt":24,"visibility":"10+","cover":"CLR","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1016,"observed":1789516380,"raw_taf":"TAF KGJT 152341Z 1600/1624 13009KT P6SM VCSH SCT070 BKN100 TEMPO 1600/1604 VRB20G35KT 5SM -TSRA BKN060CB FM160400 12009KT 6SM -SHRA SCT080 BKN120 PROB30 1604/1610 4SM TSRA BKN070CB FM161000 10008KT P6SM SCT040 BKN060 PROB30 1610/1616 4SM -SHRA BKN040 BKN045 FM161600 13007KT 6SM -SHRA SCT040 OVC080 PROB30 1616/1622 4SM TSRA BKN040CB FM162200 21007KT 6SM -SHRA SCT040 OVC110 PROB30 1622/1624 4SM TSRA BKN040CB","url":"https://av